+{"comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABRA5q2w","author":{"login":"jahnclawdmonet"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"The dimension in the traceback points at a different root than TP sharding. The mismatch is at dimension 1, which for `w13_weight` expert data (`[2 * intermediate_per_partition, hidden]`) is the hidden dim, not the TP-sharded output dim. 4096 is `hidden_size` unpacked; 2048 is the same dim NVFP4-packed at two values per byte. At TP=2 the sharded dim 0 agrees by coincidence (allocated `2*2048/2 = 2048` vs loaded shard `4096/2 = 2048`), so the first mismatch to surface is dim 1.\n\nThat arithmetic matches #36599: `DeepseekModelNextN.__init__` carries an unconditional override that nulls the quant config whenever it is `modelopt_fp4` (log line: `Overriding DeepseekV3ForCausalLMNextN quant config for modelopt_fp4 Deepseek model.`), so the draft's FusedMoE is built as unquantized BF16 modules expecting hidden 4096, while your checkpoint's MTP experts are FP4-packed at 2048. The target model is unaffected because the override lives only in the NextN path, which also explains \"identical command minus the speculative flags works\". State of this at the PR #36507 head, with the fix shape the existing resolver allows: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36599#issuecomment-5436422199\n\nA one-minute discriminator on the logs you already have, no rerun needed: grep the failing rank for `Overriding DeepseekV3ForCausalLMNextN quant config`. If it appears right before the draft load, this is #36599 in TP clothing, and the prediction is that it reproduces identically at TP=1 single node, since the dim-1 mismatch is TP-independent. That would take the sharding question out of this particular failure (your mirror-image shared-expert observation may still be worth its own audit). For what a single box can show: on sm_121 the override fires at TP=1 on the current per-model image with dummy weights; the shape crash itself needs real tensors, which do not fit on one 128 GB Spark.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-27T09:00:33Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36653#issuecomment-5436762843","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"state":"OPEN","title":"[Bug] NEXTN/MTP speculative decoding fails to load MTP MoE weights under TP>1 for Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration (GLM-5.3-Flash)","updatedAt":"2026-08-27T09:00:33Z","url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/36653"}
diff --git a/reports/j-7bfd059ec3e9/raw/upstream-pr-37322.json b/reports/j-7bfd059ec3e9/raw/upstream-pr-37322.json
